not because we just hit 100K on the channel,
- ‘WHAT?!’

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:40.769
- there will be - another video for that occasion.

00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:46.589
No today, we’re gonna once and for all show
all these other Naruto boys all those Deku

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:54.600
weebs , all those Asta nerds , why Luffy is
objectively the best Shouenen hero there is.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.379
And with objective I of course mean because
I say so with dramatic music in the background.

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:04.770
Now usually you come across 2 types of criticism
from people who have watched One Piece for

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:10.840
less than 10 seconds, when it comes to Luffy:
Luffy sucks as a main character OR Luffy sucks

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.119
as a person.

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:16.280
And so of curse, we’ll proof them wrong
on both these points.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.630
In this video I’ll show you why Luffy is
the best shounen protagonist from a storytelling

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.609
perspective and then get into his character
and what in my opinion makes it better than

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:33.720
the rest in 
a part II.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.950
Let’s go.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.390
Okay so first of all, let’s start by looking
at the premise of one piece.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:47.249
According to John Truby the premise of the
entire story boiled down to one sentence.

00:01:47.249 --> 00:01:52.560
It should contain some sort of starting point,
a sense of the Main Character and some sense

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.680
of the sending.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.680
Hm.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:02.389
So all we have to do is boil down roughly
1000 chapters of story into - one - sentence.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:06.619
I’m gonna spare you 30 minutes of me trying
to phrase this properly.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:08.030
You’re welcome.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:13.680
The premise of One Piece I would say is this:
A strong-willed and pure young man sets out

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.110
to find a crew and become the king of pirates
in order to find freedom in a world ruled

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.330
by injustice and violence.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.360
Yeah I think that works.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.970
Now on the most fundamental level the premise
is the most important part of a story.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:33.690
What you write about is way more impactful
than how you write it.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:38.451
And what makes a good premise good is not
only an interesting setting and idea, but

00:02:38.451 --> 00:02:43.280
especially a main character that goes hand
in hand with the plot.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.200
And this is what Eichiro Oda did with One
Piece.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.569
Luffy makes the story better and the story
makes Luffy better.

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:54.269
They organically enhance each other.

00:02:54.269 --> 00:02:55.629
Let me explain.

00:02:55.629 --> 00:03:00.920
As any good story, One Piece has an underlying
message that the author wants to convey.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:08.860
Now One Piece has many leading themes: Friendship,
Love, Justice, Adventure, Dreams.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:15.510
It’s a long list that I have discussed in
detail in my Iconic Scene Analysis series.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:23.230
But what is there main, the BIG and Overarching
theme of one piece?

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.330
Exactly.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:32.310
Oda has integrated all these other ideals
and values in the fundamental message of One

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:37.870
piece: Why freedom is so valuable and why
you should fight for it.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.099
The freedom to do what you want.

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:43.209
The freedom to go where you want to go.

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:46.370
The freedom to be unharmed and hurt by others.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.680
But most importantly.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.220
The freedom to be yourself.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:57.560
It’s absolutely clear that Luffy’s main
desire and drive is to reach that absolute

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.269
level of freedom.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:03.849
That may seem profound, but it’s exactly
this seamlessness, that makes the story work

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:09.890
so well, because the theme of freedom is woven
into every single part of the plot, very single

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.489
part of the world and each and every character
in the story.

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:19.420
You don’t think about it, because it’s
everywhere, the entire story is taking place

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.800
under this premise.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.630
And we’re like fish in the water.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.000
Compare this to Naruto.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:32.470
For the longest time the story makes us believe
that this is a story about how kindness and

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:36.970
courage will lead you to friendship love and
acknowledgment.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:46.240
But suddenly Naruto is the child of prophecy,
which basically completely undermined this

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:52.290
message, which is exactly why people were
so unhappy with its ending.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.840
While Naruto was the strongest Ninja in the
end, was he really the one that represented

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.070
the theme of the story best?

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:05.260
With Luffy Oda chose the most interesting
and relevant character when it comes to exploring

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.230
freedom.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.460
Luffy is the story.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.460
Literally.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:14.400
Also, I think now would be a good time to
subscribe to the chann-.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.400
‘One moment there.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.500
But what about all those weird looking villains
One Piece has.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:30.080
They’re do not badass.’

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.940
But not only Luffy embodies this central moral
argument.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.680
All of the villains and antagonists he faces
along the way, as diverse they might look

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:45.310
and as different their ambitions may be, ALL
of them, without any exception, stand opposed

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.560
to the ideal of freedom in some way or form.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:54.790
Villains like Crocodile and Doflamingo, who
control and manipulate entire countries.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:06:00.580
Villains like Caesar who capture children
to experiment on or Magellan who literally

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.590
runs a prison.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:07.790
Villains like the Tenryuubito who literally
enslave people and treat them as objects.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:13.810
And even villains like Katakuri, who is unfree
to be himself and suppressed by the high expectations

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:17.140
of his family.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:22.820
Consistency in the the main values and ideals
that are clashing in the story is such a fundamental

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.400
aspect of storytelling, but really hard to
do.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:33.810
And yet, neither the antagonists, not Luffy
ever do anything that feels out of character

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.310
and strives away from these ideals.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:41.770
This consistency represents Luffy in such
a clear and tangible way, that it makes him

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:45.660
a very 3-dimensional and authentic character.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.940
But even in his function as a main protagonist,
Luffy differs from the trope of the Shounen

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.940
hero.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:56.550
Typically, we have a main character that starts
somewhere at the bottom, giving us the typical

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:01.960
coming-of-age type of story arc, where the
protagonist is the outsider or underdog and

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.780
uses their talent or unique powers to work
their way to the top.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:13.130
Goku wants to be the strongest, Asta wants
attention and Naruto want acceptance.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:18.670
Luffy however doesn’t want to become pirate
king for any of these reasons.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.390
He simply wants to be free and happy.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:26.860
And so I would argue that the Pirate King
is quite different from the Hokages and Wizard

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:31.750
Kings out there, as they bind the heroes fulfilment
to external forces.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:39.430
It’s a goal that doesn’t require him to
become the strongest with crazy hidden powers,

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.270
but simply strong ENOUGH with he support of
his crew.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:49.970
On the other hand we have the trope of the
over-powered main character that already is

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:54.740
strong, but has to grow on a human level and
figure out a more internal struggle.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:59.840
Examples here are characters like Saitama,
Gon or Souma.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:04.200
Now, while Luffy is definitely way more advanced
with his powers at the start of the story

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:10.600
than Naruto or Deku, he is also far away from
being as over-powered as this type of character.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:15.460
Instead he is introduced with a considerate
amount of strength that then however is quickly

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:21.020
tested by stronger and stronger opponents
and open up a lot of room for growth.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:28.260
What makes Luffy so different from other heroes
then is mainly his arc in the story.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.450
Luffy doesn’t have to grow up and proof
himself to others.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:37.430
Compared to the Sasukes and Bakugos out there,
he is deeply respected by his crew and those

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:38.789
around him.

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:45.220
Luffy actually starts the story not as the
underdog, but as the captain, recruiting people

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.610
to his cause.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:53.730
In other words, his character arc not that
from boy to man, but from man to a leader.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:09:00.069
Luffy’s underlying arc to achieve his goal
is to become a better leader and captain.

00:09:00.069 --> 00:09:05.320
Given the length of the story, this development
is quite slow, which makes moments like on

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.649
Sabaody or at Marineford even more impactful
to the reader.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:16.520
Loosing his brother, Luffy doesn’t suddenly
unlocks his dark gear 6 devil awakening, but

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:21.439
breaks down in shock and trauma, as a real
person would.

00:09:21.439 --> 00:09:26.120
Now don’t get me wrong, I don’t think
either approach is better than the other.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:32.260
What matters is that this unique arc is completely
aligned with the premise of the story.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:37.389
That’s why it works so much smoother than
many other popular shows.

00:09:37.389 --> 00:09:42.620
I would say that simply form a story structure,
the setup and premise for his character puts

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.339
him way over other shounen heroes.

00:09:45.339 --> 00:09:55.230
I mean look at this.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:58.580
This is just a completely different.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.420
This IS the story.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.480
This guy unites everything that One Piece
is about.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.029
In other words, the best Shounen protagonist
out there.

00:10:08.029 --> 00:10:11.389
‘Okay listen.

00:10:11.389 --> 00:10:19.259
He may be okay from a storytelling perspective.

00:10:19.259 --> 00:10:23.310
But let’s be honest: Luffy is just so dumb
and naive.

